`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where the live sibling P7 admin pages ship (ApiPlayground,
DiskForecast, FleetTelemetryCoverage, LiveSignalInspector, SchemaDrift; apps/parity/apple-ledger.json
shows all five "done"), and which project.yml lists as a `Sources` source path. The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Admin`. This is the SAME reconciliation the SchemaDrift / DiskForecast sibling logs recorded.
Strings ship in the platform catalog `apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file).

STRING REUSE (covenant #2 — no scope narrowing, but no needless duplication / DRY): the two parity
strings already exist in the catalog from the web i18n extraction, with the EXACT web values and the
web key suffix:
    translation.orders.title    = "Active Orders"
    translation.orders.subtitle = "Vehicle orders and delivery tracking from Tesla"
The page binds those verbatim (web `useTranslation('settings')` `t('orders.title' | 'orders.subtitle')`).
The ONLY new catalog key added is `route.teslaOrders` ("Active Orders") for the sidebar route title.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the TOP-LEVEL `/tesla-orders` in the Account side-nav group
(web/src/components/layout/Layout.tsx — the "Account" group, NOT Integrations). A dedicated
`.teslaOrders` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment "tesla-orders", systemImage "cart.fill" = web
shoppingCart, group .account). No AppRouteParser alias is needed — `/tesla-orders` matches the
pathSegment on the first segment directly (verified by the executed harness below).
TeslaOrdersRouteRegistration hosts the page on that route; it is composed into `\.routeHosts` in
TeslaSyncApp.swift, so the page is reachable via the Account-group sidebar entry and any
`/tesla-orders` deep link.

@Observable BINDING (covenant #2): the web page holds NO state of its own (the manifest: "no API
data sources — renders from navigation values / local state"). Faithfully, the native page is pure
chrome that binds the embedded section's @Observable `ActiveOrdersModel` (the P1/S8 state holder) —
NOT an empty stub page-model. The page takes the model and hands it to ActiveOrdersSection(model:),
mirroring the sibling SchemaDriftPage(model:) shape.

